  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "Final rules impose strict incident reporting and customer notices, set a 7% thermal-test ceiling with 18-month remediation and no public per-model disclosure, require remote shut-off retrofit within 6 years but with a technical-feasibility escape, mandate built-in suppression at 36 months, and replace an automatic recall at 8/100k with a regulator review. Both red lines are formally satisfied, though S2 and S3 are weakened relative to the safe benchmarks and S5 leaves recall to regulator discretion."
 },
